    "body": "## What\nClarify the Wayland capture contract for distro packages versus portable Bazel addons, and document the corrected Arch recipe's Cargo cross-target and artifact dependency gate.\n\n## Why\nThe installed x86 Arch package compiled out capture despite ARM source CI enabling it. The running addon has no PipeWire dependency. This source update accompanies the separate Arch recipe repair and gives the delivered build a new normal fork identity.\n\n## Testing\nSource CI90 succeeded for head 636f1839a158b2695ce9d022cad8f51bc1b2f7c1 (native-ci step1290 exit0); merged-source CI93 also succeeded for 47d7edbf714231fe01e5536ae5ffce1f1a50f0e6 (native-ci step1294 exit0). No local native build was performed. Fork test execution remains disabled by the existing policy; CI retains checks, builds, and the compiled-version assertion. The companion recipe's five pinned archives passed SHA-256 verification; actual sysroot preparation, pkg-config target resolution, and Clang parsing of the PipeWire headers succeeded. Capture and package installation are not yet verified.\n\n---\n- [x] CI checks/build gate passes\n- [ ] Actual signed package delivered\n- [x] Existing computer-use documentation and native changelog updated\n\n## Delivery evidence\nMerged source: 47d7edbf714231fe01e5536ae5ffce1f1a50f0e6. Recipe PR65 merged as 2fa3d4fd3691297ac2bff925892df793a0af152b. Exact targeted package CI205 reached real native ARM-host x86 Cargo compilation but failed in libspa-sys bindgen because the native tooling image has no host libclang shared library. No feature fallback, signed publication, installation, or successful capture is claimed. Existing source tests/worker smoke suites remained disabled.\n",
