        "body": "## What\nReplace the portable feature-less Bazel addon with a Cargo-built x86 baseline addon using the explicit wayland-pipewire feature. Preserve native ARM CI execution, pinned x86 target libraries/headers, compiler caches, the shared fork identity/stamp, and the one-executable package build. Add libpipewire as a runtime dependency and reject an addon missing its dynamic PipeWire dependency before bundling.\n\n## Why\nThe installed addon cannot capture Wayland screens despite source CI enabling PipeWire for its separate ARM addon. Fix the actual package build path rather than retrying screenshots or changing desktop settings.\n\n## Verification\nBash syntax and ShellCheck error checks passed. Generated SRCINFO via makepkg. Downloaded all five pinned official Arch target archives and verified SHA-256 digests. Ran actual prepare(), resolved PipeWire through the resulting target pkg-config sysroot, and parsed the real PipeWire headers with Clang targeting x86_64. No local native addon build, package installation, or successful screen capture is claimed yet.\n\n## Delivery dependency\nMerge only after source documentation PR https://git.n3t.work/vith/oh-my-pi/pulls/10 passes its existing source CI gate and merges. Then build only oh-my-pi-vith-git with the exact merged source and recipe SHAs through the trusted dispatcher; verify signed publication and the installed executable. Keep the existing disabled source-test policy. Desktop permission approval remains separate.\n\n## Delivery evidence\nSource prerequisite merged as 47d7edbf714231fe01e5536ae5ffce1f1a50f0e6 after successful CI90/native-ci1290; merged-source CI93/native-ci1294 also succeeded. Recipe merged as 2fa3d4fd3691297ac2bff925892df793a0af152b. Trusted dispatch pipeline205 pinned these exact SHAs; prepare and sources passed, native step1304 failed during real ARM-host x86 Cargo compilation: libspa-sys bindgen could not locate host libclang. Superseded pipeline204 used the previous recipe22e4034 and was canceled; unrelated pipelines were untouched. PipeWire feature and dependency gate remain enabled. Signed publication, installation and actual capture remain unverified pending the host-tool prerequisite.\n",
